    "description": "OTEC Sea Surface Temperature - Annual  \n\nThe sea surface temperature is the temperature of the warm water source used by an OTEC plant. This is defined to be near the sea surface at a depth of 20 m, the approximate depth of a warm water intake pipe. \n\nSource: Ocean Thermal Extractable Energy Visualization Technical Report \n\nTemporal Info: Data from March 2009 - February 2011.",
    "description_html": "<p><strong>OTEC Sea Surface Temperature - Annual</strong>&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\n<p>The sea surface temperature is the temperature of the warm water source used by an OTEC plant. This is defined to be near the sea surface at a depth of 20 m, the approximate depth of a warm water intake pipe.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href=\"http://www.osti.gov/bridge/purl.cover.jsp?purl=/1055457/1055457.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Ocean Thermal Extractable Energy Visualization Technical Report</a>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Temporal Info:</strong> Data from March 2009 - February 2011.</p>\n",
